record raw-autotune.evidence.c5-onnx-parity-20260826/1 : evidence {
    title "C5 ONNX export parity and determinism-mode measurement"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:4e85079409d78b2072ff0efd51a54c2170fda3f2
    command ".venv-train/bin/python tools/scene_models/c5_port.py --stage parity"
    artifact "models/artifacts/c5_m7_h64.onnx"
    summary """
        C5 ONNX export parity passes. The lege-gpu-incompatible ops were decomposed (LeakyReLU to PRelu, InstanceNorm2d to ReduceMean/Sub/Pow/Sqrt/Div with biased variance matching torch, cross-pooling ReduceMax to chained elementwise Max); report.py op screen is clean. Against the unpatched upstream torch model, worst end-to-end angular gap over 30 sample inferences is 0.0001 degrees. On the 30 in-repo Sony IMX135 frames with ground-truth illuminants: 3.22 degrees mean angular error in the deterministic duplicate-own-histogram mode versus 3.25 with true sibling context — determinism costs nothing on this set. Runtime 17.8 ms CPU per frame via onnxruntime.
        """
}

record raw-autotune.evidence.camsdd-ablation-winner-20260826/1 : evidence {
    title "Phase 3b ablation: ResNet-50 @ 192x288 wins (96.92%, Backlight 90%)"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:3ec22b0e0f15001166237dc8bf36de4e9edcc9a1
    command ".venv-train/bin/python tools/scene_models/train_camsdd.py --stage finetune --arch mobilenet_v2 / --input 192x288; --stage eval --split both on ft0, ft-mnv2, ft-r50-192"
    artifact "tools/scene_models/runs/ft-r50-192/eval_both.json"
    summary """
        Phase 3b ablation on val+test (n=1200): ResNet-50 at 384x576 scored 96.67 percent top-1 with Backlight recall 82.5; MobileNetV2 at 384x576 scored 96.42 / 85.0; ResNet-50 at 192x288 scored 96.92 / 90.0 (36 of 40, exactly the Gate-2 bar). Winner: ResNet-50 at 192x288 — best overall, best Backlight, one quarter of the inference pixels. Margins are 3-6 images, so the cheaper model winning makes the choice easy. Likely mechanism: at ~330 images/class the stronger effective augmentation of RandomResizedCrop at the smaller target regularizes better than extra resolution helps.
        """
}

record raw-autotune.evidence.camsdd-adapt1-reviewed-20260826/1 : evidence {
    title "Gate 4 second round on hand-reviewed pseudo-labels: zero regression"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:3ec22b0e0f15001166237dc8bf36de4e9edcc9a1
    command ".venv-train/bin/python tools/scene_models/train_camsdd.py --stage adapt --run tools/scene_models/runs/adapt1 --init tools/scene_models/runs/ft-r50-192 --pseudo-csv .agent/scratch/camsdd-adapt/labels/pseudo-reviewed.csv --baseline 0.9750"
    artifact "tools/scene_models/runs/adapt1/metrics.jsonl"
    summary """
        Second adaptation round on the hand-reviewed pseudo-labels (43 images: the 44 conf>=0.90 labels minus the one user-review-identified Snow mislabel _DSC0887, a snowless winter road). Gate 4 passes with ZERO regression: CamSDD val top-1 recovers the full 97.50 percent baseline (adapt0 with the mislabel included had dipped one image to 97.33) — removing a single wrong training label restored the dip, at 43 images each label carries real weight. Val+test 96.83 top-1 / 99.67 top-3. Re-exported models/artifacts/camsdd_resnet50_192.onnx from adapt1 (1x3x192x288, opset 17, raw logits); report.py op screen clean (Conv/Relu/Add/MaxPool/GlobalAveragePool/Flatten/Gemm only). adapt1 replaces adapt0 as the shipping candidate.
        """
}

