        Gate 4 (phase 3c domain adaptation) passed: mixing 44 confidence-filtered (>=0.90) pseudo-labeled own-corpus proxy renders (x4 oversample) into a 5-epoch low-lr fine-tune of ft-r50-192 held CamSDD val at 97.33 percent against the 97.50 baseline (a one-image dip, inside the 0.5-point tolerance) and val+test at 96.92. Corpus effect is real but modest: high-confidence frames 44 to 49, top-1 prediction agreement 352/384, median confidence flat — the expected ceiling for one self-training round on 44 images. The larger adaptation lever is the pending human hand review of .agent/scratch/camsdd-adapt/labels/review.html (kept via akr scratch keep), which would feed a stronger second adapt round. Exported models/artifacts/camsdd_resnet50_192.onnx (1x3x192x288, opset 17) passes report.py; 36.9 ms CPU per frame.
        """
}

