record raw-autotune.evidence.harmonic-neutral-fallback-20260827/1 : evidence {
    title "Harmonic guard neutral fallback: magenta cleared, coherent frames stable"
    state superseded
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:c09b7f95cee4a97af87a4428389819203ce2c749
    command "16-frame clipped/sky corpus A/B + purple-sky question frames + night batch; before = pre-fix HEAD binary, after = neutral-fallback build"
    artifact "docs/evidence/harmonic-neutral-fallback-20260827/README.md"
    summary """
        Magenta false-colour root cause found and fixed: the joint chroma
        solve's region-global heterogeneity guard attenuated toward the
        clipped floor (chroma = clipping order, not scene). Probe at
        _DSC1334 cell (1200,600): harmonic G 1.748 (true ~1.71), guard
        output 1.146. Fix: fallback target is neutral chroma at harmonic
        luminance; discount unchanged; coherent regions unchanged. A/B:
        every changed frame improves; cloudy-sky/sunset frames 0.00%
        changed; purple-sky patch population (_DSC1282/1283/1290) clears;
        broad faint cast (_DSC1288/1289) untouched - separate cause, still
        open. Night blown screen renders neutral. 366+ tests, clippy clean,
        repeated --jobs 8 identical. Default pixels move on clipped frames:
        profile advances to archive-auto-v7.
        """
}

